course: dictionary
lesson: 15493
title: Stubbornly: refusing to give in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stubbornly means in a stubborn way. A stubborn person will not change their mind or do what others want, even when they are asked again and again. «Ruby stubbornly refused to wear her coat, even when it started to rain.» The clues are refused and even when it started to rain. Ruby would not give in, even though a coat made sense.
explain: Try the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: «Ruby refused to wear her coat, even when it started to rain, and would not change her mind.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. The word stubbornly adds the feeling that she was not going to budge.
explain: Stubbornly can also describe things, not just people. «The jam lid was stuck, and it stubbornly would not open.» A lid cannot have a mind, so here stubbornly means hard to move, change or get rid of. The clue is stuck: the lid would not budge.
fact: Stubbornly means in a stubborn way.
fact: A stubborn person will not change their mind, even when they are given good reasons.
fact: «Stubbornly» describes how something is done, so it is an adverb. The adjective is «stubborn».
fact: Things can be stubborn too: «a stain that stubbornly stays» will not come out easily.
fact: Donkeys and mules are often said to be stubborn, because they can refuse to move.
exercise: «Ruby stubbornly refused to wear her coat, even when it started to rain.» What does stubbornly mean here? | In a happy, smiling way | In a rush, very quickly | Under the table | *In a way that will not change her mind
exercise: «The stain on the carpet stubbornly stayed, however hard Dad scrubbed.» What does stubbornly show about the stain? | It was very small | It was brand new | *It was very hard to remove | It was wet and sticky
exercise: «The donkey stubbornly refused to take another step.» Which words in the sentence show that the donkey would not move? | donkey | stubbornly | *refused to take another step | sentence
test: «Mum asked me three times to tidy my room, but I stubbornly kept it messy.» What does stubbornly mean here? | Quickly and neatly | Loudly, with a song | *In a way that refuses to change, even when asked again and again | Sadly and quietly
test: «The rusty bolt stubbornly stayed in place, though Dad pulled and pulled.» What does stubbornly suggest about the bolt? | *It was very hard to move or get rid of | It was easy to pull out | It was shiny and new | It was hollow inside
exam: Ava says, «Stubbornly means the same as quickly.» What is the best reply? | *No, stubbornly means in a way that will not change or give in | No, stubbornly means very happy | Yes, they both mean fast | Yes, because both words end in -ly
